<header><p class="enc-kicker">Person</p><h1 class="enc-title">Emperor Taiwu of Northern Wei</h1><p class="enc-meta"><span class="dates">408–452</span> · Also known as Tuoba Tao</p></header>
<div class="enc-body"><p class="enc-desc">Emperor Taiwu of Northern Wei, <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/tuoba">Tuoba</a> Tao, reigned from 423 to 452. He defeated the Rouran and conquered Xia, Northern Yan and finally Northern Liang in 439, unifying northern <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/china">China</a>. Influenced by Daoist and Confucian advisers, he ordered a severe persecution of <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/buddhism">Buddhism</a> from 446. He was murdered by a <a class="enc-link" href="/encyclopedia/eunuch">eunuch</a> in 452.</p></div>
